# Shared Systems, Shell-First Delivery

Atlas shared systems must be built once, then wrapped correctly for shell and role.

- Build domain/workflow logic once in shared modules; avoid duplicating core behavior per surface.
- Add shell-specific wrappers for app and website so each experience feels native to its environment.
- Keep web and app UI/interaction patterns shell-appropriate (navigation, spacing, safe-area, fixed actions, affordances).
- When improving Personal workflows, map the same shared workflow to Client where the underlying flow is shared.
- Preserve role boundaries: shared core, role-specific presentation and access behavior.
- Prefer adapting wrappers over forking business logic when extending features.
